Install and update (Windows)
----------------------------
Keep this folder together: the setup program copies game_files\ from the
folder it runs in. Run BLiNX1-@VERSION@-setup.exe. It installs
for your user only (no administrator rights) to
%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\BLiNX1 and adds a Start Menu entry.
Running a newer setup installs on top and keeps your saves. Uninstall from
Settings > Apps; your saves and settings stay in
%LOCALAPPDATA%\BLiNX1.

Windows may warn before running the setup program or BLiNX1.exe:
they are built on your machine and not signed. SmartScreen: "More info" >
"Run anyway". If the folder came as a .zip downloaded or copied from
another machine, right-click the .zip > Properties > Unblock before
extracting (Mark of the Web), or Windows asks again for every file.

To keep saves and settings somewhere else, set BLINX1_DATA_DIR
(a Windows environment variable) to that folder before starting the game.

Options
-------
Your options live in config\config.toml in %LOCALAPPDATA%\BLiNX1.
config.default.toml, in the install folder, lists every option at its
default. Copy a line from it into your config.toml and change it there,
for example "scale = 2" under "[render]" to draw at twice the resolution.
An update replaces config.default.toml but never touches your file.

The game starts in a window. "fullscreen = true" under "[present]" in
your config.toml starts it fullscreen.

F10 (or Guide+A, or Back+L3 held for a moment) opens the in-game menu to
change these options while you play; F3 shows the frame-rate strip.
"enabled = false" under "[menu]" turns the menu off. Elite paddles do
nothing here (XInput has none). On a Steam Deck, SteamOS keeps Guide+A
for itself: use Back+L3, or bind R4 to F10 once in Steam Input (the
game's controller settings > Back Grip Buttons > R4 > Keyboard > F10).

On a Steam Deck use the steamos bundle: its README has the Deck notes.
